cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "unstated-conclusions: a library-scale audit of conclusions weaker than their proofs"
abstract: >-
  Reads the root of every proof term in a pinned Mathlib revision and asks
  whether the final step was a weakening lemma. If it was, the proof already
  established a stronger statement and discarded it; that statement is a subterm
  and arrives with its own proof. The dual of unused-assumptions, which asks the
  same question about hypotheses.
authors:
